    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d828">

                <pb facs="0834" n="830" xml:id="pg830"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/2260: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-04-20T19:00:00-05:00">April 20, 1939—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>104. Peiping’s despatch 1954, March 10,<anchor n="73" xml:id="d828-f1"/> Tsinghua
                    University. The Department suggests that in your discretion you renew your
                    representations of February 3, 1938.<anchor n="73" xml:id="d828-f2"/> You may
                    wish to review the nature and extent of the American interest in the University
                    as set forth in the Department’s 28, January 27, 1938, 7 p.m., to Peiping<anchor
                        n="73" xml:id="d828-f3"/> and to express the hope that there will be issued
                    to the Japanese military authorities in Peiping such instructions as may be
                    required to rectify the unsatisfactory situation described in Peiping’s despatch
                    under reference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
